  "reason": "With no completed experiments, the priority is to establish a clean, interpretable baseline that anchors all future comparisons. Config_013 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, no aggregation, weighted fusion) uses the simplest reasonable choice in every design dimension: PCA is a standard, computationally cheap RNA representation; Imagenet ViT-L is a strong pretrained image encoder; singleprofile avoids the added complexity of multiprofile aggregation; and weighted fusion is a simple, interpretable combination. This baseline will let subsequent experiments isolate the marginal contribution of each design axis—e.g., swapping to rna_only (config_047) or image_only (config_026) to test modality value, upgrading to multiprofile + aggregation to test whether profile complexity helps, or changing the RNA encoder to scgpt/scvi to test representation quality. Starting from the simplest multimodal configuration rather than a complex one avoids confounding multiple design choices and gives the most informative reference point under a limited budget."
}

